Output CSS:
```
function buildCss(): string {
  return lines.map((line, i) => {
    if (!checked[i]) return line
    return line.replace(UNIT_RE, (m, numS, unit) => {
      const v = convert(parseFloat(numS), unit, target, root, parent)
      return val(v, target)  // but val uses zeroUnit
    })
  }).join('\n')
}
```
But negative numbers and unitless zero handled.

