For suggestions, I need hslToRgb (exists) and luminance (exists). Let me write:
```
function suggestionFor(target: number): RGBA | null {
  const f = fgRgba.value
  const bgc = bgEff.value
  if(!f || !bgc) return null
  const {h,s,l} = rgbToHsl(f.r,f.g,f.b)
  const fLum = luminance(f)
  const bLum = luminance(bgc)
  const lighten = fLum <= bLum   // if fg darker than bg, darken further => lighten=false
  // Actually to increase contrast: if fg darker than bg (fLum < bLum), darken (l decrease).
  // if fg lighter (fLum > bLum), lighten.
  const dir = fLum > bLum ? 1 : -1
  const ratioAt = (ll:number) => { const rgb = hslToRgb(h,s,ll/100); return contrastRatio({r:Math.round(rgb.r),g:Math.round(rgb.g),b:Math.round(rgb.b)}, bgc) }
  // check endpoint
  const endpoint = dir>0 ? 100 : 0
  if(ratioAt(endpoint) < target) return null
  let lo = dir>0 ? l : 0
  let hi = dir>0 ? 100 : l
  // We want the l closest to base l that reaches target.
  // For dir>0: binary search smallest l in [l,100] with ratio>=target
  // For dir<0: largest l in [0,l] with ratio>=target
  for(let i=0;i<40;i++){
    const mid=(lo+hi)/2
    const ok = ratioAt(mid) >= target
    if(dir>0){ if(ok) hi=mid; else lo=mid } else { if(ok) lo=mid; else hi=mid }
  }
  const ll = dir>0 ? hi : lo
  const rgb = hslToRgb(h,s,ll/100)
  return {r:Math.round(rgb.r),g:Math.round(rgb.g),b:Math.round(rgb.b),a:1}
}
```
Wait for dir<0 (darken), base l is the max. We search [0,l] for largest l with ratio>=target. Binary: lo=0, hi=l. If mid ok (ratio>=target), we can go higher → lo=mid; else hi=mid. End lo is the largest ok. Good.
For dir>0, lo=l, hi=100. If mid ok, go lower → hi=mid; else lo=mid. End hi smallest ok. Good.

But there's an edge: `ratioAt(l)` at base may already be >= target (then no suggestion needed). We only call when ratio<target. Good.

hslToRgb expects s,l in 0..1, while rgbToHsl returns s,l as percentages (0-100). In existing code `hslToRgb(((h % 360) + 360) % 360, sat / 100, l / 100)`. So I must divide. In suggestionFor I wrote `hslToRgb(h,s,ll/100)` but s is 0-100 from rgbToHsl; need s/100. Fix: `hslToRgb(h, s/100, ll/100)`.

